From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:04:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hdmitx21: Dolby Vision keeps its own format on a VESA timing

Dolby Vision on the 1080p165 frame-sequential 3D base went out broken.
Player-led (low-latency) Dolby Vision is sent as YCbCr 4:2:2 12-bit,
and DRM decides that from the tunnel the DV driver asks for. The VESA
timing branch added for 3D then made every VESA output YCbCr 4:4:4,
and 4:4:4 12-bit at 1080p165 needs 601 MHz of TMDS clock, so it fell to
8-bit: the link carried 4:4:4 8-bit while the DV vendor frame and the
AVI frame stated 4:2:2, a signal no sink can show.

A VESA timing now keeps the format and depth the Dolby Vision tunnel
decided (4:2:2 12-bit for low-latency, 401 MHz on 1080p165, or the
4:4:4 8-bit container of the standard tunnel), and hdmitx21_set_display
lets a VESA timing go as YCbCr 4:2:2 as well as 4:4:4. Without Dolby
Vision nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
@@ -423,9 +423,10 @@
 
 	/* A VESA timing goes out as YCbCr 4:4:4, as the VPU makes it, when the
 	 * sink takes it, in deep colour where it takes that in 4:4:4 and the
-	 * link carries it; otherwise as RGB 8-bit
+	 * link carries it; otherwise as RGB 8-bit. Dolby Vision keeps the format
+	 * and depth its tunnel set above.
 	 */
-	if (vic >= HDMITX_VESA_OFFSET) {
+	if (vic >= HDMITX_VESA_OFFSET && !is_amdv_output_dv()) {
 		char attr_str[16];
 
 		if (attr->colorformat != HDMI_COLORSPACE_RGB &&
--- a/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hdmi_tx_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hdmi_tx_video.c
@@ -103,9 +103,10 @@
 	struct hdmi_format_para *param = &hdev->tx_comm.fmt_para;
 	int ret = -1;
 
-	/* a VESA timing goes as YCbCr 4:4:4 where DRM decided it, else as RGB */
+	/* a VESA timing goes as YCbCr where DRM decided it, else as RGB */
 	if (videocode >= HDMITX_VESA_OFFSET &&
-	    param->cs != HDMI_COLORSPACE_YUV444) {
+	    param->cs != HDMI_COLORSPACE_YUV444 &&
+	    param->cs != HDMI_COLORSPACE_YUV422) {
 		param->cs = HDMI_COLORSPACE_RGB;
 		param->cd = COLORDEPTH_24B;
 		HDMITX_INFO("VESA only support RGB format\n");
